{"dataset_label":"Mathys et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000198876"],"dataset_symbols":["DCAF12"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/DCAF12","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"DCAF12","gene_symbol_current":"DCAF12","gene_id":"ENSG00000198876","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"unclear","nucleus_padj":0.831,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0588545,"nucleus_score":-0.272364,"pct_ad":0.1154,"pct_control":0.117403,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.985617,"donor_log2fc":0.0623275,"donor_lfcse":0.0947213,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":7.1423e-06}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000198876","module":"red","kme":0.065755,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.737188,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000198876","entrez_id":["25853"],"uniprot":["Q5T6F0"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a WD repeat-containing protein that interacts with the COP9 signalosome, a macromolecular complex that interacts with cullin-RING E3 ligases and regulates their activity by hydrolyzing cullin-Nedd8 conjugates. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q5T6F0","text":"Substrate-recognition component of a DCX (DDB1-CUL4-X-box) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex of the DesCEND (destruction via C-end degrons) pathway, which recognizes a C-degron located at the extreme C terminus of target proteins, leading to their ubiquitination and degradation (PubMed:16949367, PubMed:16964240, PubMed:29779948). The C-degron recognized by the DesCEND pathway is usually a motif of less than ten residues and can be present in full-length proteins, truncated proteins or proteolytically cleaved forms (PubMed:29779948). The DCX(DCAF12) complex specifically recognizes proteins with a diglutamate (Glu-Glu) at the C-terminus, such as MAGEA3, MAGEA6 and CCT5, leading to their ubiquitination and degradation (PubMed:29779948, PubMed:31267705). Ubiquitination of MAGEA3, MAGEA6 by DCX(DCAF12) complex is required for starvation-induced autophagy (PubMed:31267705). Also directly recognizes the C-terminal glutamate-leucine (Glu-Leu) degron as an alternative degron in proteins such as MOV10, leading to their ubiquitination and degradation. Controls the protein level of MOV10 during spermatogenesis and in T cells, especially after their activation (PubMed:34065512)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}